# Template Sync Ignore File
# ============================================================
# Files and folders listed here will NOT be synced from the
# upstream template (jpawlowski/hacs.integration_blueprint).
#
# Syntax follows .gitignore glob patterns.
# See: https://github.com/AndreasAugustin/actions-template-sync
# ============================================================

# ── Your integration source code ─────────────────────────────
# Never overwrite your integration with blueprint placeholder code
custom_components/

# ── Tests ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Test files reference your integration domain (set by initialize.sh).
# Future test files added by the blueprint would arrive with
# ha_integration_domain hard-coded, breaking your imports.
tests/

# ── Project configuration ─────────────────────────────────────
# These files are customized for your integration during initialization
# (initialize.sh replaces ha_integration_domain and related strings).
# Syncing them back would revert those substitutions.
pyproject.toml
.yamllint.yml
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# ── Ignore pattern files ───────────────────────────────────────
# .gitignore and .prettierignore contain a domain-specific negation pattern
# (!custom_components/<your_domain>/) set by initialize.sh that cannot be
# expressed as a generic placeholder. Syncing would revert that line.
.gitignore
.prettierignore

# ── Runtime dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────
# requirements.txt lists your integration's PyPI dependencies (synced with
# manifest.json → requirements). This is user-owned content.
requirements.txt

# requirements_test.txt pins pytest-homeassistant-custom-component, and that
# package in turn pins one exact Home Assistant version (0.13.325 → 2026.4.4,
# 0.13.354 → 2026.8.0). .github/dependabot.yml already excludes the package
# because it is bumped by hand together with hacs.json "homeassistant", and
# hacs.json is owned here as well (listed below). A sync bypasses that policy
# and silently moves the test environment to an HA version this integration does
# not declare — as #64 did, proposing 0.13.354 against a hacs.json that still
# said 2026.4.0. Both were raised together afterwards, by hand.
# Trade-off: a test dependency the blueprint newly adds to this file has to be
# copied over by hand — `script/compare-blueprint` shows what changed. Losing
# the PHCC bumps is the point, not a cost.
requirements_test.txt

# ── Dependency pins Dependabot keeps ahead of the template ────
# Dependabot bumps these here on its own schedule, so this repo is structurally
# ahead of the blueprint and a sync can only ever propose a downgrade. It has
# already cost twice: #21 needed a follow-up commit to undo a colorlog
# regression, and #47 was closed unmerged because five of its six files were
# rollbacks. Trade-off: tooling the blueprint newly adds has to be copied over
# by hand — `script/compare-blueprint` shows what changed.
requirements_dev.txt
package.json
package-lock.json

# ── Spell-check coverage ─────────────────────────────────────
# Widened in #48 to cover AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and docs/, and to drop the
# DEPENDENCIES.md this repo deleted. codespell exits 0 on paths that do not
# exist, so a sync would not fail here - it would silently stop checking three
# of the five targets.
script/spell
script/spell-check

# ── Scripts this repository has fixed ahead of the blueprint ──
# script/hassfest calls activate_venv *before* detecting the Home Assistant
# version, because the detection imports homeassistant and only resolves inside
# the venv (03ffecd). The blueprint still activates it afterwards and #77
# proposed that revert wholesale, comment and all. Owned here until the fix
# lands upstream.
script/hassfest

# script/lint, script/lint-check and script/yaml-check were owned here while
# the architecture-check and zizmor gates the blueprint wires in still failed
# on this repository. #80 and #81 fixed the underlying findings, so all three
# are back to the blueprint's own versions and sync again.

